{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789425853,"nonce":"Woxyt+GMqntmlq1vzo0lbRg1C5U=","title":"wasm AOT: compile a program to one .wasm through LLVM, linked by wlift itself","message":"Today the browser gets the whole VM as a wasm-bindgen cdylib and runs Wren source. The second distribution is Ash's: `wlift --aot game.wasm --target wasm32-wasip1 game.wren` emits one core module with the compiled program and the runtime inside, and nothing else has to be installed. Route: MIR -\u003e LLVM IR -\u003e wasm32 object -\u003e wlift's own linker, against a runtime object prelinked when wlift is built (ash: crates/ash_wasm_link, docs/aot.md#webassembly, docs/wasm/*.md).\n\nStages, in order. Each ends with a test that runs under wasmtime.\n\n1. Runtime object. Build wren_lift as a wasm32-wasip1 staticlib with the AOT entry points and every wren_* helper but no host feature (a portable `aot_runtime` feature split from `aot`, which today implies cranelift/host). Prelink with rust-lld -r plus wasi-libc into wlift_runtime.o beside the wlift binary; a freshness test fails naming the first missing export.\n\n2. Target layouts. object_layout.rs holds 64-bit literal offsets. Add a Layout table per pointer width chosen from the target triple, assert the wasm32 side under wasmtime the way the 64-bit side is asserted natively. Lowering, constants and the bootstrap read the table, never offset_of!.\n\n3. LLVM AOT lowering. An AOT mode of llvm_backend: helpers as declared externals by symbol, module variables and constants as data symbols, the bootstrap main mirroring emit_aot_bootstrap_main (wlift_aot_new_vm, init_prelude, alloc_const_string, enter/exit), TargetMachine for wasm32-wasip1, write_to_file(Object). Trampolines per distinct signature for dynamic calls: wasm has no registers and checks every indirect call's signature (ash docs/wasm/abi.md). Functions that yield take the MIR state-machine transform before lowering, so Fiber works in compiled frames from the start; the link-time unwind/rewind transform is 407f14a.\n\n4. Linker. A crate that links exactly two relocatable objects: the program object and wlift_runtime.o. Six index spaces, twelve relocation types, data and shadow-stack layout, TLS, constructors, exports (main, wlift_module_init), reachability sweep keeping all data. Refuse what it does not implement (COMDAT, 64-bit relocations, PIC). Verify every patch site holds the object-local index the symbol table says before writing. Test by differential comparison against wasm-ld, not by inspection.\n\n5. Hosts. `wlift wasm run prog.wasm` under wasmtime; `wlift wasm prog.wasm` inspects and `--validate` names missing imports; the browser harness loads an AOT module through a WASI preview-1 shim next to the VM build.\n\n6. Roots. Wasm locals are not in linear memory, so the conservative scan sees only spills. Explicit roots for pointer-bearing values live across calls in a linear-memory shadow frame (407f14a item 1), scoped roots for Rust pointers held across an allocating call. Optimisation must not promote a rooted value out of the frame.\n\nLater, on this base: the fiber transform (407f14a), the one-agent scheduler and thread module, isolates as Workers (d51592b), CI building the wasm arm of the corpus under wasmtime with the fibers-on arm last.\n\nParent epic: 6923f6e.","files":null}]}